{"v":3,"src":"MOV     AX, 1015h        ; read one DAC register\nMOV     BX, 1            ; register 1: what text colour 1, blue, shows\nINT     10h              ; DH = red, CH = green, CL = blue, 0..63\nMOV     [RED1], DH\nMOV     [GRN1], CH\nMOV     [BLU1], CL\nMOV     AX, 0920h        ; a bar of 20 blanks...\nMOV     BX, 001Fh        ; ...on page 0, white on blue\nMOV     CX, 20\nINT     10h\nMOV     BH, 0            ; page 0\nMOV     AX, 0E0Dh        ; BIOS teletype: CR...\nINT     10h\nMOV     AX, 0E0Ah        ; ...and LF: on to the next line\nINT     10h\nCALL    WAIT1            ; a second of blue\nMOV     AX, 1010h        ; set one DAC register\nMOV     BX, 1\nMOV     DH, 63           ; red\nMOV     CH, 32           ; green\nMOV     CL, 0            ; blue: together, orange\nINT     10h\nCALL    WAIT1            ; a second of orange\nMOV     AX, 1010h        ; the old colour back\nMOV     BX, 1\nMOV     DH, [RED1]\nMOV     CH, [GRN1]\nMOV     CL, [BLU1]\nINT     10h\nMOV     AH, 09h\nMOV     DX, OFFSET MSG1\nINT     21h\nMOV     AL, [RED1]\nCALL    PHEX2\nMOV     DL, \" \"\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nMOV     AL, [GRN1]\nCALL    PHEX2\nMOV     DL, \" \"\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nMOV     AL, [BLU1]\nCALL    PHEX2\nMOV     AH, 09h\nMOV     DX, OFFSET CRLF1\nINT     21h\n\nRED1    DB      0\nGRN1    DB      0\nBLU1    DB      0\nMSG1    DB      \"DAC 1 was $\"\nCRLF1   DB      13, 10, \"$\"\nWAIT1:                   ; wait 1 s: CX:DX = 0F4240h microseconds\nMOV     CX, 000Fh\nMOV     DX, 4240h\nMOV     AH, 86h\nINT     15h\nRET\nPHEX2:                   ; print AL as two hex digits; changes AX, CX, DX\nPUSH    AX\nMOV     CL, 4\nSHR     AL, CL           ; the high nibble first\nCALL    PDIG1\nPOP     AX\nAND     AL, 0Fh          ; then the low one, falling into PDIG1\nPDIG1:\nADD     AL, \"0\"\nCMP     AL, \"9\"\nJBE     PDIG2\nADD     AL, 7            ; \"A\"..\"F\"\nPDIG2:\nMOV     DL, AL\nMOV     AH, 02h          ; DOS: print DL\nINT     21h\nRET","seg